WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:05.337
First: an exemption's
expiry date has passed.

3
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:06.350
What happens?

4
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:10.220
The answer is b: it's kept for
the record but no longer honored,

5
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.775
and the guide reports expired
exemptions every month.

6
00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:17.750
Second: when is a finding this
guide addresses ready for closure?

7
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:22.125
The answer is b: when every applicable
control state has evidence.

8
00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:25.304
The authorizing official
or assessor decides;

9
00:00:25.304 --> 00:00:28.075
a pass in an assessment
isn't the decision.

10
00:00:28.075 --> 00:00:33.050
The module page has three more questions,
each linked to the unit that answers it.
